SUMMARY:Grandmother Redwood at Jack London
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nIt's time to hike at Jack London. We'll visit 
 the enormous Grandmother Redwood tree. Stop at Camp Via\, hike up the old 
 orchard. The trails will take us through mixed forest\, redwood groves\, o
 ak woodlands\, and grassy meadows. Best for individuals with at least a mo
 derate level of fitness.\n\n**\\*Important Notice\\***\nIf you've enjoyed 
 hiking with this group follow me as I move Go Wild Hikers to a new platfor
 m by the end of May\, called Heylo at - [https://heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX
 ](https://heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX)\nClick on the link above to join.\n\n
 **Where We Meet/Important Directions**\nJack London State Park\n2400 Londo
 n Ranch Rd\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\nAfter passing **entrance/pay kiosk** m
 ake a right to upper parking lot.\nGive yourself enough time to arrive\, u
 se the restroom & pay park fee. It often takes longer than you think.\n\n*
 *The Hike (Group Hike #343)**\nMountain\, Quarry\, Vineyard\, Camp Via\, A
 pricot Tree\, Apple Tree\, New Fallen Bridge\, Old Fallen Bridge and Lake 
 trails - A lollipop route.\nLength - 5.5 miles/8.9 kilometers\nElevation c
 hange - 800 feet/244 meters\nDifficulty - 7 out of 10 - Moderately easy\nE
 xposure - 30% sun / 70% shade - some steep rocky sections\, ticks/insects 
 and poison oak.\nBring plenty of water. At least 68 oz./2 liters.\nDogs - 
 Not permitted.\nFacilities at trail head - Shade\, picnic tables and toile
 ts.\nCost - $5 cash.\nParking - $10 State Park fee or free with State Park
  Pass.\nRemember to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water\
 , a hat\, a snack/lunch and layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scent
 ed products the day of a group hike!\nOf course\, we will all look out for
  each other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their own safety a
 nd well-being during hikes.\n\n**After Hike Coffee/Food**\nLes Pascals (Fr
 ench bakery)\n13758 Arnold Dr\, Glen Ellen\, CA 95442\n[(707) 934-8378](ht
 tps://www.google.com/search?q=french+bakery+glen+ellen&oq=french+bakery+Gl
 en+ellen&gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUqDAgAECMYJxiABBiKBTIMCAAQIxgnGIAEGIoFMhAIARAuG
 K8BGMcBGIAEGI4FMgYIAhBFGEAyCAgDEAAYFhgeMggIBBAAGBYYHjIICAUQABgWGB4yCggGEAA
 YgAQYogTSAQg5OTUwajBqN6gCCLACAfEFED_C7AGwjrs&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8#)\n[
 https://www.lespascalspatisserie.com/](https://www.lespascalspatisserie.co
 m/)\nOR\nGlen Ellen Village Market\n13751 Arnold Dr. Glen Ellen\, CA 95442
 \n[(707) 996-6728](https://www.google.com/search?gs_ssp=eJzj4tVP1zc0zCpISs
 8ozMo2YLRSNaiwMLAwMTW2NDRITjMyMDdKsTKoSE40STM3Nk1NSjZIMUlKSvQSTM9JzVNIzQGR
 uYlF2aklAA5OFmE&q=glen+ellen+market&oq=glen+ellen+market&gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvb
 WUqEAgBEC4YrwEYxwEYgAQYjgUyCggAEAAY4wIYgAQyEAgBEC4YrwEYxwEYgAQYjgUyBwgCEAA
 YgAQyCAgDEAAYFhgeMggIBBAAGBYYHjIICAUQABgWGB4yCAgGEAAYFhgeMggIBxAAGBYYHjIIC
 AgQABgWGB4yCAgJEAAYFhge0gEINzkyN2owajeoAgiwAgE&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8#)\
 nhttps://glenellenvillagemarket.org/\n\n**When We Meet**\nSunday May 17\, 
 2026\n8:30 am - 12:00 pm\nIf your plans change after you sign up even if y
 ou're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Attend if you are
  sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested positive for Covi
 d-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be changed\, rescheduled or cancell
 ed in case of excessive heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, zombie apocaly
 pse etc... Check your email the night before for any possible changes.
