 M-2FBrlew7aw9m6nTRse0ZnQqkOF-2FmXiyzA7UY7RLs5DXHegozj1Cn2gBVIqUcyF01GGur-2
 FpsbuaIxAEj-2FxkCPXl-2FDAXz4GZR2dqmJ2pEwYb7FwrkUj3K4MHU3Jv1T0uHrMgu2Gtcjy1
 oWuAj9a0P1fOZ6MgnlNfXzTB8vlnwzQATLAGEGaZ6tTOsjPnnXYQ6c6qZTlgf4L4J3HYa-2BjV
 kmLJjtyD3FlKBISyaxvg84yV4xubj7p97uQ1s4qepMweZdnzHrp77I8YLFrMx4hp83o-3D)\n\
 nClick on the link above to join for free. It just takes a few clicks to c
 reate your profile.\nHappy trails\, this is not the end but the beginning 
 of a different trail for Go Wild Hikers. Come and Hike with us. Zoli\nBack
  to the current Hike.\n\n**Where We Meet/Important Directions**\nMoore Cre
 ek Park\n2602 Chiles Pope Valley Rd\, St Helena\, CA 94574\n**Carpool if y
 ou can - This is a very Popular Park!**\nSouth on Hwy 128 past Calistoga -
  Left on Deer Park Rd (Sign Pacific Union College) - Right on Silverado Tr
 ail - Left on Sage Valley Rd/Hwy 128 - Past Lake Hennessey - Pay Attention
  - Left on Chiles Pope Valley Rd - Left into Moore Creek Park past a priva
 te house on a very narrow road there is a large parking lot.\nGive yoursel
 f plenty of time to arrive. It's often farther than you think.\n\n**The Hi
 ke (Group Hike #344)**\nChiles Creek\, Whiskey Ridge\, Conn Peak and Shore
 line trails\, - a lollipop hike\nAllTrails Map -\nhttps://www.alltrails.co
 m/explore/recording/lake-hennessey-e70981f\nDistance - 6 miles/9.7 kilomet
 ers\nElevation change - 900 feet/274 meters\nDifficulty - 6+ out of 10 - M
 oderate\nExposures - 30% sun/70 % shade - creek crossing\, poison oak\, ti
 cks/insects.\nBring plenty of water. At least 68 oz./2 liters.\nDogs - Yes
 \, friendly dogs on a leash are permitted at Lake Hennessey section (this 
 hike). But they're prohibited in Moore Creek (different hike).\nFacilities
  at trail head - Port O Potti\nCost - Suggested $5 cash donation. No one t
 urned away!\nParking - Free - Napa Ag & Open Space welcomes donations.\nRe
 member to wear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water for your d
 og too\, a hat\, a snack/lunch and layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use An
 y scented products the day of a group hike!\nOf course we will all look ou
 t for each other but ultimately\, hikers are responsible for their own saf
 ety and well-being during hikes.\n\n**After Hike Gathering?**\nThe Calisto
 ga Creamery\n1473 Lincoln Avenue\, Calistoga 94515\nCome to the Calistoga 
 Creamery to enjoy organic ice cream and organic frozen yogurt\, thick cust
 om milk shakes\, root beer floats and sundaes. No high fructose corn syrup
 \, artificial colors or flavors. No hydrogenated oils and no GMOS.\n\n**Wh
 en We Meet**\nSaturday May 23\, 2026\n8:30 am - 12:00 pm\n**Carpool if you
  can - This is a very Popular Park!**\nIf your plans change after you sign
  up even if you're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Atte
 nd if you are sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested posi
 tive for Covid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be changed\, reschedul
 ed or cancelled in case of excessive heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, z
 ombie apocalypse etc... Check your email the night before for any possible
  changes.
